{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792707637,"nonce":"rTPyHW1mdTtc6AM91FUCyfbwfkM=","title":"Exit with a tier-up compile in flight: embedder contract, and the zynml CLI","message":"zynode, zypy and zylua now all end a run by flushing output and calling _exit (zynode: e8b35471 and 72a97b54; zypy and zylua already had exit_now). Still open:\n\n1. zynml's CLI returns normally from main after run_file, so with its llvm-backend option it presumably has the same delay or crash at exit; unverified, no test.\n2. Embedders have no non-waiting way to stop. TieredRuntime::shutdown joins the promotion workers, so an embedder that drops the runtime waits out a compile in flight, and one that exits normally races LLVM's static destructors. Needed: a documented quiesce that does not wait (invalidate queued promotions, set a cancel flag checked under the compile lock, and in any follow-up or deferred build), with the contract that the host leaves through _exit. A cancel check inside a running LLVM compile is not possible; Ash records compiles of 0.5 s to 51 s.\n3. Not every exit goes through the helper: zypy and zylua do not wrap a panic in the program thread. zynode now does.\n\nSurvey of Ash and Rayzor behind this (read from the code, not run): Ash leaves through _exit after flushing stdout, stderr and C stdio, leaks the interpreter and sets a process-wide abandon flag checked under the compile lock; its own error, panic and out-of-memory paths still exit normally, so they can wait or crash, and unclosed guest file buffers are lost at _exit. Rayzor has no _exit: a normal return joins every queued compile through the broker's FIFO shutdown (the same wall time), and guest exit and uncaught exceptions call plain exit while a compile runs. History in Ash: a wait on the compile fixed a crash of about 9 in 100 runs (the JIT listener's destructor against codegen), then _exit replaced the wait.\n\nMeasured with the fix (NUC, release, --llvm): a 120-function program's median exit delay after its output went from 1,088 ms to 2 ms; with the handler-running exit swapped back in, the new test (tests/exit.rs, release with llvm-backend) fails because the process does not exit successfully.","files":null}]}